    "title": "Jumanji: Open World shares first trailer and plot details at CinemaCon",
    "text": "Published Apr 14, 2026, 6:41 AM EDT Jumanji: Open World promises an action-packed Christmas Day Jumanji 3 title revealed at CinemaCon along with plot details Photo: Sony Pictures Sign in to your Polygon.com account As revealed at CinemaCon 2026, the next Jumanji movie is called Jumanji: Open World. Like previous Jumanji movies, this wacky action-adventure should come with a fresh batch of video game monsters, silly jokes, and jungles to explore, though based on pictures from the set, the story will also take us to an urban, real-world setting this time. Welcome to the concrete jungle! While Jumanji: Open World is the third installment in the Jumanji series directed by Jake Kasdan, following Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle from 2017 and Jumanji: The Next Level from 2019, it's the fifth Jumanji movie ever made. The original Jumanji, a cult classic starring Robin Williams, was released in 1995. The latest film will include a tribute to Williams, and it will also feature one-half of the iconic dice from the original movie. According to the still-unreleased trailer shown to audiences at CinemaCon, the chaos brought by the Jumanji games has crossed over to the real world, with natural disasters — including ostriches running wild — hitting towns. The four main actors will play different versions of their \"avatar characters,\" adding a further layer of chaos to the adventure. If that weren't enough, Johnson's Dr. Smolder Bravestone now speaks with a Spanish accent.",
